  "body": "## What changed\n\nA setup now picks the work offset its program runs in (G54..G59), builds on #325 (merged).\n\n- **Storage:** `SetupDef.work_offset: Option<usize>`. `None` = **Auto**, the inferred per-operation law every older document posted with (first slot the op's heights reference, else G54). New setups also start on Auto, so existing fixtures and goldens post byte-identically.\n- **One law:** `posting::wcs_slot::wcs_slot(world, setup, params)` reads the setup's pick first. `wcs_context` and all of its callers follow it (generation, stamp, spindle law, machine travel check, single-file / per-op / script post, the #315 rotation clause).\n- **Command:** `SetSetupWorkOffset`, undoable and validated at construction (setup exists, slot < 6, not the current value). A datum transfer copies the source's pick.\n- **UI:** the Setups page has a \"Work offset\" combo under each setup (Auto, G54..G59). It queues the command and never writes the world itself.\n- **Project v51:** the setup payload carries `\"work_offset\": \"G55\"`, left out when nothing is picked. v50 files step up with absent = Auto. An unknown word is a corrupt file. The version bump makes older readers refuse the file instead of posting a G55 setup at G54.\n- **Refusals by name:**\n  - In the verification gate: an op whose heights are measured from a different slot than its setup's pick (`Face1: its heights are measured from G56 but setup Setup1 posts at G55 - ...`).\n  - In the one-file / script post: two setups posting the same word from different placements (`setups Setup1 and Setup2 both post at G54 from different placements ... pick another work offset for Setup2 ..., or post one file per operation`). Per-op files are exempt because each file belongs to one setup.\n  - Note: the one-file refusal also catches documents that pick nothing. Before this change they posted that case silently.\n- **Setup sheet:** WCS OFFSETS ends with `program offset: G55 (picked for this setup)` or `program offset: per operation - ... (not picked)`.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/196-setup-wcs.md`\n\n## Readings\n\n- A G55 pick at (10, 20, 5) gives the same program as G54 at the origin except for the G-word and the coordinates. Every X/Y/Z in the program (not counting the G28 home lines) shifts by exactly (-10, -20, -5).\n- Milling stamps do not read the program origin, so a pick leaves milling paths fresh. Turning kinds go stale through the spindle-origin stamp (#62), as they did before.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/setup_wcs.rs` (new, 7 tests):\n  - `a_picked_offset_posts_its_word_and_moves_coordinates_by_exactly_the_offset`\n  - `the_pick_undoes_and_redoes_exactly`\n  - `a_datum_transfer_carries_the_pick`\n  - `the_pick_round_trips_and_old_files_read_the_inferred_law`\n  - `a_height_on_another_slot_than_the_pick_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `two_setups_on_one_word_from_different_placements_refuse_one_file`\n  - `the_setup_sheet_names_the_program_offset`\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_wcs_tests.rs`:\n  - `the_picker_sets_the_setups_work_offset_through_the_command`: kittest; combo click, G55, then Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Y.\n  - `a_refused_pick_changes_nothing_and_says_why`\n- `probe_op`: the version pin is updated from 50 to 51.\n\n## Quick gate (local, debug)\n\n- **App suites, all green:** posting, setups, wcs_align, project_roundtrip, commands_undo, conformance, golden_cl (goldens unchanged), fanuc_post, rotated_wcs, setup_sheet, probe_op, lathe_spindle_law, machine, per_op_files, scripting, setup_wcs, plus the app lib.\n- **UI lib (CWD crates/ui):** 287 tests, all green. No snapshot changed: the picker only draws on a document that has setups.\n- **Clippy:** `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --tests -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nChangelog: A setup picks its work offset (G54-G59, default Auto = inferred per operation) on the Setups page; every op of the setup posts at it, the setup sheet names it, and conflicting picks are refused by name (project v51)\n\nFixes #196\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
